ISO-10303-21;
/* M193: TRIANGULATED_FACE whose geometric_link references a real ADVANCED_FACE entity (#37, own PLANE/EDGE_LOOP geometry) that is never itself wired into any CLOSED_SHELL/OPEN_SHELL/MANIFOLD_SOLID_BREP reachable from the shape representation; input: AP242 file where a tessellated face declares an exact-BRep counterpart that the reader transfer graph never visits, so the geometric_link entity is syntactically present but never bound in the transient-process map; wired as a direct shape_representation item (own COORDINATES_LIST, no GEOMETRIC_CURVE_SET wrapper) to isolate the fallback from the GEOMETRIC_SET GRI-fallback-path instability that crashes OCCT for M022/Pmi164/probe-equivalent bare-GEOMETRIC_CURVE_SET layouts regardless of geometric_link content; StepToTopoDS_TranslateFace.cxx:718-738 looks up the link via aTP->Find() (a lookup, not a recursive translate), finds no binder, and falls back to a fresh empty TopoDS_Face with theHasGeom cleared -- a face genuinely lacking a B-Rep surface, giving BRepCheck_Face::Blind NoSurface check a live target; mirrors M022 (which used geometric_link=$, the absent case, not the unresolvable-reference case); covers stp-tess-dangling-brep-link (face subvariant) + bc-no-surface in one fixture; live-verified: occt=shape(1)/shape(1) clean (face[0].surface_type=="other", brepcheck.valid==False -- NoSurface genuinely fires), gmsh=signal(11) on BOTH this fixture and a minimal fully-resolved control (geometric_link=$, no dangling ref) -- the gmsh crash is inherent to gmsh independent-OCC-build processing of any surfaceless tessellated-only face, not an artifact of the unresolved-link defect itself; synonyms: tessellated face dangling geometric_link, unresolved exact-BRep counterpart, fresh empty face on unbound link, TESSELLATED_FACE geometric_link unbound, NoSurface fallback face from tessellation */
HEADER;
FILE_DESCRIPTION(('M193'),'2;1');
FILE_NAME('M193.stp','2026-07-12T00:00:00',(''),(''),'cad-research-suite','','');
FILE_SCHEMA(('AP242_MANAGED_MODEL_BASED_3D_ENGINEERING_MIM_LF { 1 0 10303 442 1 1 4 }'));
ENDSEC;
